.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-DELETE-RECORD 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-delete-record \- remove the records of one type at one name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds delete-record
.BR \-\-zone | \-z
.I ZONE
[\fB\-\-name\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR]
.BR \-\-type | \-t
.I TYPE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a record set: every record of one type at one name. Records of
other types at the same name stay.
.PP
To remove one value and keep the rest, write the rest with
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1)
instead.
.PP
Once the last record at a name is gone, the name answers NXDOMAIN \-
unless a wildcard covers it, or names below it still have records, in
which case it answers with no records but without NXDOMAIN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
The record's name, written as for
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1).
Defaults to the apex.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
The record type. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The record set was removed.
.TP
.B 1
No such zone in your account, no records of that type at that name
(HTTP 404), a name outside the zone, or a grant does not allow it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds delete-record --zone corp.example --name api --type AAAA
euclid-cli eds delete-record --zone corp.example --type TXT
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-delete-zone (1)
